      <memberdef kind="variable" id="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_graph_collect_row_1a868e06cff836b616dd04817bc5c054a5" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>std::vector&lt; std::size_t &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::vector&lt;std::size_t&gt; AGRemapCore::GraphCollectRow&lt; K, V, KeyHash, KeyEqual &gt;::blocks</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>blocks</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::GraphCollectRow::blocks</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Which branch of each ``if`` block the part sits in within its own `section`_, outermost first: the
position, among the section&apos;s parts, of the ``if`` / ``else if`` / ``else`` line that opens the branch.
It names the same branches as \ref guards, but tells apart two branches whose tests read the same -- two
parts share a branch exactly when one&apos;s list starts with the other&apos;s. Always filled
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
